ce for travel and tourism is  you and i have discussed  many countries have cabinet officials  in charge of tourism we don't even have  an assistant secretary now i'm not a big  government guy but as you know when  you're in  in in the debates within the federal  agencies you need  someone senate confirmed to  uh stand up for this huge part of our  economy  which goes across so many states can you  share with me a little bit of your  perspective of the importance of this  act it passed out of this committee  very strongly every senator but one  voted for it and we're gonna try and  move it again quickly this year  yes thank you for your question and and  for your leadership on on this  issue um you're right we're the only one  of the top 30  global destinations that doesn't have a  cabinet level  uh uh person and or an arm that actually  goes out and promotes travel that's why  we have brand usa so  uh we believe very much that the  leadership is needed um we've been very  pleased with secretary raimondo's um  interest in how important travel and  tourism is to the  industry but obviously she has many  things to to focus on so we couldn't  agree with you more  um that we'd like to see your bill  introduced uh again quickly and passed  and we've already also raised with the  secretary  the importance of elevating this  position so uh  hopeful that we will will be able to  move it forward  um it's also something that we've talked  to the travel and tourism advisory board  at the national travel tourism office  at the department of commerce about and  believe that  that with this type of leadership to to  really be able to draw that interagency  group together  um that we can um set that national  strategy to reopen  um not only domestic travel but bring  back international travel  bring back meetings and events we need  the whole of the industry  um focused upon and having a cabinet  level position would absolutely help do  that  great thank you my next question is for  you  and miss dover i i want to talk a little  bit about the cruise ship industry and  and you know a lot of times the industry  gets attacked for certain issues but  what i really want to talk about  is how important this industry  is to small businesses whether in  florida or  in alaska and um if you can give us a  sense on that but also  uh miss barnes i saw that um the u.s  travel association  recently called for the cdc to end its  ban on cruise ship travel  in america that's uh what our bill  senator scott  and my bill the cruz act that we  introduced today  would do and and they need the guidance  and look the cdc  does a good job on the science they've  had a tough year  an important agency my state has worked  hard  dealing with the health issues we've  been the number one state in the country  throughout the pandemic in terms of  testing per capita  in terms of the vaccination rates per  capita we're proud of that in alaska  fortunately one of the lowest death  rates per capita  but my state's economy is getting  crushed  oil and gas no
 

